firmware: xilinx: export zynqmp_pm_invoke_fn() from zynqmp-core.c

Stable commit 69baa01c94101 ("remoteproc: xlnx: Check remote core state")
adds EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(zynqmp_pm_invoke_fn) to drivers/firmware/xilinx/zynqmp.c
so that modular users (e.g. the remoteproc and crypto drivers) can link.

Downstream main split zynqmp.c into zynqmp-core.c / zynqmp-pm.c / ... and
drivers/firmware/xilinx/zynqmp-pm.c was resolved to the downstream side, so the
export hunk was dropped together with the stable copy of the function.
Re-add the export next to the downstream definition in zynqmp-core.c.

diff --git a/drivers/firmware/xilinx/zynqmp-core.c b/drivers/firmware/xilinx/zynqmp-core.c
--- a/drivers/firmware/xilinx/zynqmp-core.c
+++ b/drivers/firmware/xilinx/zynqmp-core.c
@@ -677,6 +677,7 @@
 	va_end(arg_list);
 	return ret;
 }
+EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(zynqmp_pm_invoke_fn);
 
 /**
  * zynqmp_pm_load_pdi_word_swap - Perform word swapping on a memory address.
